Houlihan Lokey, Inc. (NYSE:HLI) is a leading global investment bank recognized for delivering independent strategic and financial advice to corporations, financial sponsors, and governments. With uniquely deep industry expertise, broad international reach, and a partnership approach rooted in trust, the firm provides innovative, integrated solutions across mergers and acquisitions, capital solutions, financial restructuring, and financial and valuation advisory. Our unmatched transaction volumes provide differentiated, data-driven perspectives that help our clients achieve their most critical goals. To learn more about Houlihan Lokey, please visit HL.com.&#xa;&#xa;Capital Solutions
Houlihan Lokey’s Capital Solutions Group was named World’s Best and Europe’s Best for Capital Markets Advisory at the Euromoney Awards for Excellence 2026. The group comprises more than 235 professionals globally and offers clients a broad range of tailored financing alternatives and strategic financial advice. Our team has raised ~$37bn across over 140 transactions in the last twelve months*and has a presence in 18 offices and 8 countries globally. With deep expertise in both private and public markets, we are committed to delivering innovative, value-enhancing solutions that support long-term success for our clients.&#xa;&#xa;Job Description
A Summer Associate in the Real Estate, Lodging & Leisure Investment Banking Group in the New York office will work on a variety of active engagements, business development assignments, and growth initiatives. The group offers a unique opportunity for Associates to work on a variety of projects that provide exposure to various financial advisory and investment banking products and sectors within the real estate industry. The Associate will have the following tasks:
Prepare, analyze and help explain historical and projected financial information;
Coordinate and perform business due diligence and execute M&A and capital raising transactions;
Prepare confidential information memoranda, management presentations, marketing pitches and other presentations;
Value real estate companies, businesses, and assets;
Assist in the marketing and planning of engagements; and
Build relationships and maintain direct contact with clients, prospective clients and professional advisors.
Basic Qualifications
The ideal candidate would possess the following qualities and background:
An undergraduate degree, including an exemplary academic record, from an accredited institution;
An MBA degree from a top accredited institution with a graduation date between December 2027 and June 2028;
Candidates should have experience executing transactions and interpreting / structuring legal agreements;
Advanced accounting, finance, financial modeling and analytical abilities;
Nuanced understanding of real estate valuation theory, methodologies and applications;
Excellent verbal and written communication skills, including experience interacting with clients and/or potential investors;
Be an independent thinker and resourceful problem solver driven to succeed;
Have a very strong work ethic, organizational skills and ability to multitask; and
A demonstrated ability to work cooperatively with all levels of staff.
Teamwork is essential to the firm’s success. At the same time, creativity and new ideas are encouraged. Associates are given substantial responsibility and are encouraged to help us grow our business. The ideal candidate should be motivated, creative, outgoing, and possess strong communication and financial analysis skills.
Candidates must have a strong knowledge of accounting and applied financial theory, keen analytical capabilities, and excellent verbal and written communication skills.
